  "graph": {
    "name": "TCS: GeoSpatial Data Analysis Using TCS Digital Platform for NextGen Agriculture DNA",
    "link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Dxq_U1TNx1s",
    "categories": "data_ingestion, compute_intensive",
    "graph_usable": true,
    "notes": "GeoSpatial data analysis (329 hectares of area) for agriculture related usecases - soil health, yield, etc. Sources:\n    1. Open Source satellite data by ISRO and NASA.\n    2. Registry of Open Data provided by Amazon in an S3 bucket. They are using it because this reduces data transfer costs. Also this data is already well preprocessed.\n    3. Data coming from field agents and managers.\n    SageMaker is used because of the parallel execution of jobs in it -- provides much needed scalability.\n    CloudFront helps cache the data to provide better user experience and reduce transfer costs when maps are consumed by the users."
  },
